WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:09.350
Hilary Clinton's new book "What Happened"
hit stores on September 12th and her

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:13.280
publisher promised that she will let
loose about her experience as a woman in

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.070
politics in a way that she's never done
before. Will it help her poll numbers? I

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:21.860
doubt it. Throughout the 2016 campaign, both

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:26.390
Clinton and Donald Trump were viewed
negatively by most voters. That's still

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:31.550
true today. In a new NBC News / Wall Street
Journal poll, only thirty percent had a

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.830
positive view of her, while 53 percent
had a negative one. Trump's numbers were

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:41.210
similar. Hillary did best in public
opinion polls when she was a senator

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:46.339
from New York, and when she was Secretary
of State. But questions about her honesty,

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:51.019
her establishment ties, and an
unexpectedly vigorous challenge from

00:00:51.019 --> 00:00:56.150
Bernie Sanders hurt her 2016 candidacy.
Hillary Clinton says she is letting her

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:59.839
guard down with her new book, and she
takes some shots at Sanders and Joe

00:00:59.839 --> 00:01:05.299
Biden in it. But it's unlikely to improve
her poll numbers. That's a difficult task.

00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:10.969
To learn more about my take on Hillary
Clinton, check the links in the

00:01:10.969 --> 00:01:15.049
description below. Also, let us know what
other topics you want our scholars to

00:01:15.049 --> 00:01:20.460
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

